WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.179 --> 00:00:05.618
Hi, welcome back to Nagarjuna,

00:00:05.618 --> 00:00:09.701
Arya Nagarjuna, and we
stopped at this point here.

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:15.747
We were talking about how do
causes create their results.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:19.144
We reached a part called

00:00:19.144 --> 00:00:22.328
RGYUS 'BRAS BU SKYE BA'I
BYA BA SBYOR BA BYED PA

00:00:22.328 --> 00:00:27.126
How is it exactly that a
cause triggers a result.

00:00:27.126 --> 00:00:32.126
And then we're going to
discuss whether or not a cause

00:00:32.149 --> 00:00:35.407
can exist in and of itself.

00:00:35.407 --> 00:00:39.324
This is all part of an
idea of a discussion

00:00:40.269 --> 00:00:44.519
about the possibility that
causes and their results

00:00:45.768 --> 00:00:47.709
are not one and the same thing,

00:00:47.709 --> 00:00:50.808
that they are separate things.

00:00:50.808 --> 00:00:52.829
Which would we normally say?

00:00:52.829 --> 00:00:53.989
Is the cause the result

00:00:53.989 --> 00:00:57.158
or are the cause and result separate?

00:00:57.158 --> 00:01:00.424
What would we normally say?

00:01:00.424 --> 00:01:01.529
Yeah. Separate.

00:01:01.529 --> 00:01:04.997
If the cause was the result, then

00:01:04.997 --> 00:01:07.049
I wouldn't have to be here today

00:01:07.049 --> 00:01:10.217
because I already prepared the class.

00:01:10.217 --> 00:01:12.100
That would be the class.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:14.419
So now we're going to
discuss the possibility

00:01:14.419 --> 00:01:17.618
that the cause and the
result are discreet entities,

00:01:17.618 --> 00:01:19.031
or separate from one another.

00:01:19.031 --> 00:01:21.249
Can they be separate things?

00:01:21.249 --> 00:01:22.199
And that's a little trickier

00:01:22.199 --> 00:01:25.111
because that's what we normally think.

00:01:25.111 --> 00:01:29.919
And there are places in this book

00:01:29.919 --> 00:01:31.871
where Choney Lama, in my opinion,

00:01:31.871 --> 00:01:36.498
is scrambling to make an outline.

00:01:36.498 --> 00:01:38.940
He's trying to make logical sense

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:43.500
out of Nagarjuna's poetry,
especially the whole flow.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:46.260
So he has sort of

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:50.677
a very interesting move
here, like a basketball move.

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:54.800
He says the way I see it

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:57.421
you can impose an outline on this section

00:01:57.421 --> 00:01:59.468
called 'The Seven Reasons

00:01:59.468 --> 00:02:02.730
Why Cause and Their Results
cannot be Separate'.

00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:04.811
Seven Reasons Why Causes and Their Results

00:02:04.811 --> 00:02:06.411
Cannot be Separate.

00:02:06.411 --> 00:02:09.392
So he's going to go
through seven sections now

00:02:09.392 --> 00:02:11.843
and he's going to point out
seven problems with the idea

00:02:11.843 --> 00:02:14.764
that causes and their
results are separate.

00:02:14.764 --> 00:02:19.689
And personally, I can remember
when I reached this section.

00:02:21.113 --> 00:02:24.421
It felt like he was repeating himself.

00:02:24.421 --> 00:02:26.103
It felt like ideas were coming up

00:02:26.103 --> 00:02:29.415
that had already been treated before.

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:31.095
And I checked and I checked and

00:02:31.095 --> 00:02:35.695
what I believe is what
we had discussed before

00:02:35.695 --> 00:02:39.195
was mainly in the context of the convening

00:02:40.103 --> 00:02:43.045
of the causes and conditions.

00:02:43.045 --> 00:02:45.903
When the causes and
conditions come together,

00:02:45.903 --> 00:02:48.593
what is their relationship to the result?

00:02:48.593 --> 00:02:50.584
And now he's taking the causes out of

00:02:50.584 --> 00:02:52.983
the convening of the causes and conditions

00:02:52.983 --> 00:02:56.093
and he's saying, what's
the specific relationship

00:02:56.093 --> 00:02:59.514
between the cause in
isolation and its result?

00:02:59.514 --> 00:03:01.733
The cause independent of the convening

00:03:01.733 --> 00:03:04.163
of the causes and conditions.

00:03:04.163 --> 00:03:06.064
But you're going to
hear the same arguments

00:03:06.064 --> 00:03:07.144
and then you're going to get confused

00:03:07.144 --> 00:03:10.075
because you're going to think
we covered them already.

00:03:10.075 --> 00:03:14.133
Seven different possibilities here.

00:03:14.133 --> 00:03:17.715
There's a major mistake
in the Tibetan carving

00:03:17.715 --> 00:03:20.875
which took a while to figure out,

00:03:20.875 --> 00:03:23.125
and we'll discuss it.

00:03:25.142 --> 00:03:28.725
Here's the seven. I'll say them quickly,

00:03:31.125 --> 00:03:33.270
And we'll talk about it.

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:36.129
Possibility number one:
the result is triggered

00:03:36.129 --> 00:03:39.728
by a cause which has already stopped,

00:03:39.728 --> 00:03:43.145
but it is somehow still present.

00:03:44.109 --> 00:03:47.560
Number two: the result is triggered,

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:50.758
and in Tibetan and in Sanskrit they say

00:03:50.758 --> 00:03:52.658
"in sight of the cause,"

00:03:52.658 --> 00:03:55.248
meaning the cause can somehow look ahead

00:03:55.248 --> 00:03:56.736
and see a result coming.

00:03:56.736 --> 00:04:01.129
I like to call it anticipation,
He calls it in sight,

00:04:01.129 --> 00:04:03.577
in sight of the cause.

00:04:03.577 --> 00:04:05.289
The result is in sight of the cause,

00:04:05.289 --> 00:04:07.129
meaning the cause is like this

00:04:07.129 --> 00:04:08.612
and he can see the cause.

00:04:08.612 --> 00:04:10.297
He can see the result coming.

00:04:10.297 --> 00:04:13.797
That's another possibility.

00:04:13.797 --> 00:04:18.797
And in that case would the cause
and the result be separate?

00:04:18.836 --> 00:04:21.420
Like that, in a discussion.

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:24.940
Third possibility that
the result is triggered:

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:27.398
we're going to discuss whether
the result is triggered

00:04:27.398 --> 00:04:30.398
by contact with the cause or not.

00:04:30.398 --> 00:04:34.731
Can there be contact
between cause and result?

00:04:36.229 --> 00:04:38.765
And that's a difficult question. Because?

00:04:38.765 --> 00:04:42.375
By the time the result
comes out the contact is...

00:04:42.375 --> 00:04:43.456
the cause is gone.

00:04:43.456 --> 00:04:45.634
So how can they ever make contact?

00:04:45.634 --> 00:04:46.658
If they don't make contact,

00:04:46.658 --> 00:04:50.158
why couldn't that same cause cause a pizza

00:04:51.067 --> 00:04:54.140
that you're going to buy me tonight?

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:55.723
As just an example.

00:04:56.628 --> 00:05:01.628
Number four is

00:05:03.017 --> 00:05:06.215
the cause void of the result

00:05:06.215 --> 00:05:08.646
in the time of the cause or not?

00:05:08.646 --> 00:05:11.948
Is the result somehow present
in the time of the cause

00:05:11.948 --> 00:05:16.558
within the cause, as
potential, for example.

00:05:16.558 --> 00:05:18.817
Fifth possibility,

00:05:18.817 --> 00:05:22.734
and this is where the
Tibetan carving went off.

00:05:25.028 --> 00:05:28.611
Does the fact of the
result being triggered

00:05:31.118 --> 00:05:34.646
have an inherent cause and
result contained within it?

00:05:34.646 --> 00:05:37.697
That's where the Tibetan goes off.

00:05:37.697 --> 00:05:39.685
It's difficult. We'll talk about it.

00:05:39.685 --> 00:05:43.958
Possibility number six: is the
result triggered by a cause,

00:05:43.958 --> 00:05:47.164
when the result is triggered by a cause

00:05:47.164 --> 00:05:48.798
is the cause the same as the result

00:05:48.798 --> 00:05:50.216
or separate from the result?

00:05:50.216 --> 00:05:51.686
We already said they were separate

00:05:51.686 --> 00:05:54.148
but he's going to go there.

00:05:54.148 --> 00:05:59.131
Number seven: is the result
which is triggered by a cause,

00:06:00.038 --> 00:06:02.838
does it have its own nature or not?

00:06:02.838 --> 00:06:05.977
What's the status of the result?

00:06:05.977 --> 00:06:07.365
So let's go through them one by one

00:06:07.365 --> 00:06:09.106
and you'll see.

00:06:09.106 --> 00:06:13.148
To say all seven of those
in a row is too much.

00:06:13.148 --> 00:06:14.758
Sorry.

00:06:14.758 --> 00:06:18.008
Here's possibility number one.

00:06:18.008 --> 00:06:20.776
To repeat, option number one of the seven,

00:06:20.776 --> 00:06:24.909
or mini examination, mini investigation,

00:06:24.909 --> 00:06:28.217
was: is it possible that a result

00:06:28.217 --> 00:06:30.658
is triggered by a cause

00:06:30.658 --> 00:06:32.433
that has to stop first

00:06:32.433 --> 00:06:35.082
and then the result comes?

00:06:36.149 --> 00:06:37.709
Got it?

00:06:37.709 --> 00:06:41.278
That's how we normally think of things.

00:06:41.278 --> 00:06:43.278
Like the seed stops and the tree starts,

00:06:43.278 --> 00:06:45.110
something like that.

00:06:45.110 --> 00:06:48.310
So he's going to examine is it possible

00:06:48.310 --> 00:06:50.979
that the result is triggered by a cause

00:06:50.979 --> 00:06:54.468
where that cause has already
stopped, technically,

00:06:54.468 --> 00:06:56.438
because it became the result.

00:06:56.438 --> 00:06:58.938
That's another question.

00:07:00.430 --> 00:07:03.800
And here, if you're reading the Tibetan,

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:06.539
Nagarjuna uses the word NUB PA

00:07:06.539 --> 00:07:09.339
for 'stopped', for the cause.

00:07:09.339 --> 00:07:13.688
And NUB PA means

00:07:13.688 --> 00:07:15.990
for the sun to go down,

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:18.127
or for the Dharma to
disappear in the world.

00:07:18.127 --> 00:07:21.666
These are the verb, this is the verb.

00:07:21.666 --> 00:07:25.666
And he's used that verb for the cause.

00:07:27.758 --> 00:07:30.347
Does the cause disappear
behind the horizon

00:07:30.347 --> 00:07:32.539
before the result comes out?

00:07:32.539 --> 00:07:35.667
That's the way he wants to say it.

00:07:35.667 --> 00:07:37.227
,'BRAS BU SKYES PA JI LTAR SKYED,

00:07:37.227 --> 00:07:38.185
How could that be?

00:07:38.185 --> 00:07:40.351
,'BRAS BU DANG NI 'BREL BA'I RGYU,

00:07:41.634 --> 00:07:46.301
So how could the cause stop
and then produce the result?

00:07:47.926 --> 00:07:49.967
Because there wouldn't be any relationship

00:07:49.967 --> 00:07:51.788
between cause and effect

00:07:51.788 --> 00:07:55.288
because it's a principle of Buddhist logic

00:07:56.316 --> 00:07:58.658
that for two things to have a relationship

00:07:58.658 --> 00:08:01.447
they both have to be existing.

00:08:01.447 --> 00:08:02.955
Duh!

00:08:02.955 --> 00:08:05.356
What are the two possible
kinds of relationships?

00:08:05.356 --> 00:08:07.106
That's another story.

00:08:08.711 --> 00:08:10.711
Well I'll tell you.

00:08:12.472 --> 00:08:15.070
No, that's another story, long story.

00:08:15.070 --> 00:08:17.750
Anyway, for two things
to have a relationship

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:21.632
they both have to be
in the room, basically.

00:08:21.632 --> 00:08:23.152
And if one of them has already disappeared

00:08:23.152 --> 00:08:27.763
then there's no discussion
of a relationship.

00:08:27.763 --> 00:08:29.146
,'BRAS BU DANG NI 'BREL BA'I RGYU,

00:08:29.146 --> 00:08:30.779
,GNAS PAS KYANG NI JI LTAR SKYED,

00:08:31.662 --> 00:08:35.752
But if you're saying that the
cause is somehow still around

00:08:35.752 --> 00:08:38.192
by the time the result comes out,

00:08:38.192 --> 00:08:41.609
then there's a problem there also.

00:08:43.622 --> 00:08:45.752
Then there would be a piece of the result

00:08:45.752 --> 00:08:48.693
that was existing in the time of the cause

00:08:48.693 --> 00:08:51.254
before the result had occurred.

00:08:51.254 --> 00:08:55.391
If they ever, if they touch
anywhere, there's a problem.

00:08:55.391 --> 00:08:57.403
If the cause happened in 2011

00:08:57.403 --> 00:08:59.654
and the result happened in 2012,

00:08:59.654 --> 00:09:01.144
and somehow they touch each other

00:09:01.144 --> 00:09:05.525
then, what was it, midnight
on the 31st of December

00:09:05.525 --> 00:09:09.843
and they shared a 10 minutes?
They stretched somehow?

00:09:09.843 --> 00:09:12.563
And if they never make contact

00:09:12.563 --> 00:09:15.602
then anything could cause anything

00:09:15.602 --> 00:09:18.263
because there's no necessary contact

00:09:18.263 --> 00:09:19.703
between the cause and the result.

00:09:19.703 --> 00:09:22.714
Then any result could
come out of any cause.

00:09:22.714 --> 00:09:24.539
,CI STE RGYU 'BRAS MA 'BREL NA,

00:09:24.539 --> 00:09:26.397
,'BRAS BU GANG ZHIG SKYED PAR BYED,

00:09:27.242 --> 00:09:28.205
And that's the whole argument.

00:09:28.205 --> 00:09:33.205
So you see a picture here of
a rabbit coming out of a hat.

00:09:34.763 --> 00:09:36.063
I was trying to find something

00:09:36.063 --> 00:09:38.445
where you had a result without a cause,

00:09:38.445 --> 00:09:40.925
with no visible cause around.

00:09:40.925 --> 00:09:43.594
So that's kind of the feeling here.

00:09:43.594 --> 00:09:46.122
We don't know where the rabbit came from.

00:09:46.122 --> 00:09:49.375
The rabbit wasn't in the
hat the moment before.

00:09:49.375 --> 00:09:51.903
There was no rabbit of the moment before.

00:09:51.903 --> 00:09:54.925
Somehow he just popped out.

00:09:54.925 --> 00:09:58.054
It's almost an effect without a cause.

00:09:58.054 --> 00:09:59.882
A result without a cause.

00:09:59.882 --> 00:10:02.615
That's what the picture
is supposed to indicate.

00:10:02.615 --> 00:10:07.461
So this first option is
that the cause has stopped

00:10:07.461 --> 00:10:08.775
and then the result comes.

00:10:08.775 --> 00:10:11.975
And that's kind of how
we feel instinctively

00:10:11.975 --> 00:10:14.485
about how cause and effect works.

00:10:14.485 --> 00:10:18.253
I agree the cause and effect
can't exist at the same time.

00:10:18.253 --> 00:10:21.945
That gets messy. But
how about if the cause

00:10:21.945 --> 00:10:24.603
just goes up to a certain place and stops

00:10:24.603 --> 00:10:27.974
and then the result
starts. Can't we say that?

00:10:27.974 --> 00:10:32.342
And he says, well, then you've
got a result without a cause,

00:10:32.342 --> 00:10:34.642
which is not possible,

00:10:34.642 --> 00:10:38.225
which is like a rabbit
coming out of a hat.

00:10:40.842 --> 00:10:43.411
I got very uncomfortable at this point

00:10:43.411 --> 00:10:45.634
and I had a deep realization,

00:10:45.634 --> 00:10:48.354
which I've been thinking
about for a couple of days.

00:10:48.354 --> 00:10:53.337
Nowhere in this book does
he tell you an option.

00:10:55.973 --> 00:10:57.602
Nowhere in this... he only,

00:10:57.602 --> 00:10:59.451
it's like only complaining about your wife

00:10:59.451 --> 00:11:03.362
and never making a positive suggestion.

00:11:03.362 --> 00:11:04.611
You know what I mean?

00:11:04.611 --> 00:11:07.710
The whole book is saying
what things are not.

00:11:07.710 --> 00:11:09.726
Even the opening verse is

00:11:09.726 --> 00:11:10.867
SKYE BA MED PA, CHAD MED PA (SIC)

00:11:10.867 --> 00:11:13.287
Like this
MED PA MED PA MED PA MED

00:11:13.287 --> 00:11:15.046
With no
YOD PA

00:11:15.046 --> 00:11:20.046
He doesn't describe the option to nothing

00:11:20.566 --> 00:11:23.267
which is dependent origination.
He never goes there.

00:11:23.267 --> 00:11:26.987
Nobody in this book goes
to a real explanation

00:11:26.987 --> 00:11:31.518
of mental seeds and projections
and things created by...

00:11:31.518 --> 00:11:36.507
There's no explanation in
this root text or commentary,

00:11:36.507 --> 00:11:38.958
specific explanation of
how we create things,

00:11:38.958 --> 00:11:41.649
like the pen explanation.
It's missing here.

00:11:41.649 --> 00:11:45.211
And it gets scary here.

00:11:45.211 --> 00:11:47.629
It gets uncomfortable for the audience

00:11:47.629 --> 00:11:51.109
because now he's saying it's not possible

00:11:51.109 --> 00:11:56.109
that the cause could stop and
then a result come out of it.

00:11:56.131 --> 00:11:57.619
And it's also not possible that the cause

00:11:57.619 --> 00:12:00.531
could not stop and the result come out.

00:12:00.531 --> 00:12:05.330
And then, and he keeps saying by nature.

00:12:05.330 --> 00:12:07.419
These things cannot happen by nature.

00:12:07.419 --> 00:12:09.699
These things don't happen
from their own side.

00:12:09.699 --> 00:12:12.188
These things don't
happen self-existentingly

00:12:12.188 --> 00:12:14.739
but he never tells you what's the option.

00:12:14.739 --> 00:12:17.110
He never tells you what it would be like

00:12:17.110 --> 00:12:22.110
for something to start
through mental seeds

00:12:22.658 --> 00:12:24.590
or through dependence. He never tells you.

00:12:24.590 --> 00:12:26.499
He just tells you
throughout what they're not.

00:12:26.499 --> 00:12:29.259
The whole book is a not book.

00:12:29.259 --> 00:12:31.469
It's like a bad day with
your partner or something.

00:12:31.469 --> 00:12:34.291
They just keep telling
you, they don't say:

00:12:34.291 --> 00:12:36.139
"I like this"... They're
just: "I don't like this,

00:12:36.139 --> 00:12:37.691
I don't like this."

00:12:37.691 --> 00:12:38.658
And you get to the end of the book

00:12:38.658 --> 00:12:41.130
and he didn't say he liked anything.

00:12:41.130 --> 00:12:44.099
And so I thought here let's
look at the ice cream,

00:12:44.099 --> 00:12:46.731
which is very important to me.

00:12:46.731 --> 00:12:51.706
And this is a very
extremely important picture

00:12:54.708 --> 00:12:56.889
for the rest of your life.

00:12:56.889 --> 00:13:01.430
So this is how causes
really are creating effects.

00:13:01.430 --> 00:13:03.361
This is how it really happens.

00:13:03.361 --> 00:13:06.270
Because nobody in the
whole book tells you.

00:13:06.270 --> 00:13:08.690
He just keeps saying what's not true.

00:13:08.690 --> 00:13:12.539
And he wants us to struggle.
He wants us to think:

00:13:12.539 --> 00:13:14.950
Well, what's really going on?

00:13:14.950 --> 00:13:16.771
And he never tells us.

00:13:16.771 --> 00:13:18.830
He just keeps saying it's
not this. It's not this.

00:13:18.830 --> 00:13:20.909
It's not this. And you'll see

00:13:20.909 --> 00:13:23.179
he just keeps saying that.

00:13:23.179 --> 00:13:27.299
There's no chapter called
the chocolate sauce.

00:13:27.299 --> 00:13:31.120
So here we go. The white ice cream

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:34.378
represents the parts of a thing,

00:13:34.378 --> 00:13:36.811
like the parts of a car,

00:13:36.811 --> 00:13:38.961
or the parts of a pen. You guys got a pen?

00:13:38.961 --> 00:13:40.771
I've got a pen.

00:13:40.771 --> 00:13:44.021
Pens and tight jeans don't go together.

00:13:48.319 --> 00:13:51.603
I can get it out. I just want to prove it.

00:13:51.603 --> 00:13:56.603
So,

00:13:56.944 --> 00:13:58.739
the pen of yesterday

00:13:58.739 --> 00:14:01.499
didn't cause the pen of today,

00:14:01.499 --> 00:14:06.499
or the factory, the pen factory,

00:14:07.120 --> 00:14:09.481
which is the cause, didn't make this pen.

00:14:09.481 --> 00:14:12.659
This pen was not a result of a pen factory

00:14:12.659 --> 00:14:15.881
in Japan or something like that.

00:14:15.881 --> 00:14:17.822
Well so what's really going on?

00:14:17.822 --> 00:14:21.255
Well either the factory closed

00:14:21.255 --> 00:14:24.891
and the pen came out.

00:14:24.891 --> 00:14:27.819
The cause stopped and
then the pen came out.

00:14:27.819 --> 00:14:29.681
They stopped that day's production

00:14:29.681 --> 00:14:31.830
and then tomorrow the pen came out.

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:33.961
Or the pen came out at the end of the day

00:14:33.961 --> 00:14:36.041
and then they all went home.

00:14:36.041 --> 00:14:38.291
And the factory... that's it.

00:14:39.176 --> 00:14:41.506
The factory that made this
pen is no longer there.

00:14:41.506 --> 00:14:44.407
Maybe tomorrow's factory is there.

00:14:44.407 --> 00:14:46.952
And then the other possibility is that

00:14:46.952 --> 00:14:48.941
the exact factory that made this pen

00:14:48.941 --> 00:14:52.072
is still doing the same
thing it made this pen with

00:14:52.072 --> 00:14:55.655
on this pen, while the
pen's already there.

00:14:56.550 --> 00:14:58.501
The factory's still making this pen

00:14:58.501 --> 00:15:00.512
after Geshe-la's writing with this pen.

00:15:00.512 --> 00:15:03.428
That's the other possibility.

00:15:03.428 --> 00:15:05.678
So what's really happening?

00:15:07.370 --> 00:15:10.796
So yesterday we went out for
TSE BCU. We had ice cream.

00:15:10.796 --> 00:15:14.511
There was gelato, two kinds of gelato:

00:15:14.511 --> 00:15:16.561
strawberry and vanilla.

00:15:16.561 --> 00:15:21.510
And then they think of those

00:15:21.510 --> 00:15:24.940
as the parts of the pen.
So here's the strawberry.

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:26.801
There's the ball of strawberry gelato.

00:15:26.801 --> 00:15:29.384
Here's the ball of...

00:15:30.358 --> 00:15:32.708
Here's the ball of vanilla gelato.

00:15:32.708 --> 00:15:35.416
And then you put them both in a bowl

00:15:35.416 --> 00:15:37.788
and then you pour
chocolate sauce over them.

00:15:37.788 --> 00:15:39.978
And that's kind of how we create things.

00:15:39.978 --> 00:15:42.077
There's a bottom half of the pen.

00:15:42.077 --> 00:15:44.218
There's the upper half of the pen.

00:15:44.218 --> 00:15:48.507
They are there. They are
there when we enter the room.

00:15:48.507 --> 00:15:52.650
And then our mind
perceives these two pieces

00:15:52.650 --> 00:15:56.850
and then a seed opens in my mind

00:15:56.850 --> 00:15:58.009
and a picture comes out.

00:15:58.009 --> 00:15:59.578
I like to call it a luminous picture

00:15:59.578 --> 00:16:02.978
because it... On the day that you see

00:16:02.978 --> 00:16:05.488
pictures coming out of your mind,

00:16:05.488 --> 00:16:08.821
they will look like neon pictures, neon.

00:16:10.068 --> 00:16:12.408
They are bright. They are luminous.

00:16:12.408 --> 00:16:14.758
They are artificially bright.

00:16:14.758 --> 00:16:17.279
The picture of a pen
doesn't look like this.

00:16:17.279 --> 00:16:20.428
When a mental seed opens for pen,

00:16:20.428 --> 00:16:22.719
what comes out of your mind is

00:16:22.719 --> 00:16:27.719
an impossibly well-defined,
neon picture of a pen.

00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:31.908
And then that flies, there's
even a physical sensation

00:16:31.908 --> 00:16:35.079
of that seed, that image, luminous image,

00:16:35.079 --> 00:16:37.508
flying out of your mind,
somewhere in your forehead,

00:16:37.508 --> 00:16:39.908
which is weird, but that's the way it is,

00:16:39.908 --> 00:16:41.890
and it lands on the objects.

00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:45.399
It lands on the pieces
and it unifies them.

00:16:45.399 --> 00:16:49.288
And then the dog has a different picture

00:16:49.288 --> 00:16:51.718
coming out of their karmic seeds.

00:16:51.718 --> 00:16:54.448
And that's a picture of a chew toy

00:16:54.448 --> 00:16:57.636
and it lands on the same
two balls of ice cream

00:16:57.636 --> 00:17:02.528
and coats them, and then it
becomes a, what do you call it?

00:17:02.528 --> 00:17:03.696
Fudge.

00:17:03.696 --> 00:17:06.198
Fudge sundae or something.

00:17:06.198 --> 00:17:08.345
So and it is a kind of coat.

00:17:08.345 --> 00:17:10.607
That's why I chose this picture.

00:17:10.607 --> 00:17:11.988
I used to use a different picture

00:17:11.988 --> 00:17:14.247
that had kind of skinny
streams of chocolate

00:17:14.247 --> 00:17:16.567
and I wasn't satisfied with it.

00:17:16.567 --> 00:17:19.018
When you really see it happen,

00:17:19.018 --> 00:17:23.748
it'll be almost a complete
coating, but not quite.

00:17:23.748 --> 00:17:28.698
So it will look like chocolate
sauce poured on ice cream.

00:17:28.698 --> 00:17:31.378
When you finally see it yourself,

00:17:31.378 --> 00:17:35.887
which is within a few hours
of seeing emptiness directly,

00:17:35.887 --> 00:17:38.935
you'll see your mind
making these pictures.

00:17:38.935 --> 00:17:41.186
So that's what's really happening.

00:17:41.186 --> 00:17:44.175
There's a cause, which is a seed.

00:17:44.175 --> 00:17:47.435
There's a result, which is a tree.

00:17:47.435 --> 00:17:49.556
And the relationship between them

00:17:49.556 --> 00:17:54.531
is an artificial creation
of your mental seeds.

00:17:55.386 --> 00:17:58.346
And that cause and effect relationship

00:17:58.346 --> 00:18:01.386
is the chocolate sauce. And
the two balls of ice cream

00:18:01.386 --> 00:18:03.556
are the seed and the tree.

00:18:03.556 --> 00:18:06.074
What bothers Nagarjuna

00:18:06.074 --> 00:18:08.735
is that without the chocolate sauce,

00:18:08.735 --> 00:18:11.407
there is no, there
cannot be a relationship

00:18:11.407 --> 00:18:13.287
because if they touch
somewhere then that part

00:18:13.287 --> 00:18:17.076
is ice cre... vanilla and strawberry --

00:18:17.076 --> 00:18:18.887
and that's not possible.

00:18:18.887 --> 00:18:21.055
So either they touch or they don't touch.

00:18:21.055 --> 00:18:24.076
If they do touch, it's
a third thing going on.

00:18:24.076 --> 00:18:27.396
If they don't touch, then how
can they be cause and effect?

00:18:27.396 --> 00:18:30.066
Because they never meet each other.

00:18:30.066 --> 00:18:35.066
Then the answer, the punchline
is that your mental seeds

00:18:35.774 --> 00:18:39.107
are throwing out like a parachute shape

00:18:40.076 --> 00:18:42.447
and that covers the
two balls of ice cream,

00:18:42.447 --> 00:18:45.047
the cause and effect,
and your mind creates

00:18:45.047 --> 00:18:46.934
the cause and effect relationship;

00:18:46.934 --> 00:18:51.351
an illusion of a cause
and effect relationship.

00:18:53.255 --> 00:18:54.985
So that's what's really
going on and they never,

00:18:54.985 --> 00:18:58.485
I don't believe they're ever
going to say it in the book.

00:18:58.485 --> 00:19:00.087
So I thought it would
be nice to say it here

00:19:00.087 --> 00:19:02.336
because it's frustrating.

00:19:02.336 --> 00:19:05.016
The punchline is almost always the same:

00:19:05.016 --> 00:19:07.448
the cause cannot touch the result

00:19:07.448 --> 00:19:11.605
because then there would
be a point of contact

00:19:11.605 --> 00:19:14.688
where the result existed in the past.

00:19:16.205 --> 00:19:18.666
And they can't not touch because then

00:19:18.666 --> 00:19:21.885
that particular seed could cause a pizza

00:19:21.885 --> 00:19:25.096
or inflation, or

00:19:25.096 --> 00:19:27.685
just weird stuff that's
not connected to it.

00:19:27.685 --> 00:19:28.786
But they can't be connected

00:19:28.786 --> 00:19:30.826
because then they have to
exist in the same time.

00:19:30.826 --> 00:19:35.466
If they are connected in
any way, "relationship",

00:19:35.466 --> 00:19:39.014
then a piece of one has to be in the past

00:19:39.014 --> 00:19:40.586
or a piece of the other
has to be in the future

00:19:40.586 --> 00:19:41.736
and that's not possible either.

00:19:41.736 --> 00:19:44.005
So it gets frustrating, nobody tells you,

00:19:44.005 --> 00:19:46.203
and then he just goes on.

00:19:46.203 --> 00:19:47.684
It gets frustrating. So yeah,

00:19:47.684 --> 00:19:51.896
the answer is: your mind
is creating the connection

00:19:51.896 --> 00:19:53.426
between cause and effect.

00:19:53.426 --> 00:19:56.093
Your mind is seeing a connection

00:19:57.205 --> 00:20:01.365
where someone else's mind
might not see a connection.

00:20:01.365 --> 00:20:05.782
And for them the connection
might be different.

00:20:07.045 --> 00:20:09.325
And that's a cool thing.

00:20:09.325 --> 00:20:14.226
The punchline, but the super
punchline is that that's proof

00:20:14.226 --> 00:20:16.565
that you have to be nice to other people.

00:20:16.565 --> 00:20:19.026
And by the way if someone explains to you

00:20:19.026 --> 00:20:21.325
the emptiness of cause and effect

00:20:21.325 --> 00:20:23.906
and doesn't talk about
being nice to other people,

00:20:23.906 --> 00:20:27.279
I don't believe they understand it.

00:20:27.279 --> 00:20:28.398
I don't believe they understand it.

00:20:28.398 --> 00:20:29.918
If they're not talking about morality

00:20:29.918 --> 00:20:31.668
within three minutes,

00:20:32.628 --> 00:20:34.289
then they don't really understand.

00:20:34.289 --> 00:20:36.639
Because the natural question

00:20:36.639 --> 00:20:39.690
of any human being would be

00:20:39.690 --> 00:20:41.423
"I like two balls of ice cream

00:20:41.423 --> 00:20:43.257
and chocolate sauce, Geshe-la.

00:20:43.257 --> 00:20:44.367
How do I get it?"

00:20:44.367 --> 00:20:47.076
How do I make it happen?

00:20:47.076 --> 00:20:51.996
And if the cause and effect

00:20:51.996 --> 00:20:55.588
ice cream sauce theory is correct,

00:20:55.588 --> 00:20:58.228
and you understand it,

00:20:58.228 --> 00:21:00.858
the next question you should be asking me

00:21:00.858 --> 00:21:05.527
is how do I make the right sauce to get

00:21:05.527 --> 00:21:07.474
a million dollars?

00:21:07.474 --> 00:21:10.680
And stop working so hard. Right, Osiris?

00:21:10.680 --> 00:21:13.332
How can I just take care of that?

00:21:13.332 --> 00:21:15.500
And if you don't ask that question,

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:20.029
then I'm suspicious that you
don't understand the point,

00:21:20.029 --> 00:21:24.092
which is if my karmic seeds
are creating the sauce

00:21:24.092 --> 00:21:26.052
that combines cause and effect,

00:21:26.052 --> 00:21:29.012
how can I create more sauce for money

00:21:29.012 --> 00:21:33.670
or for love or for good
health or for mental peace,

00:21:33.670 --> 00:21:37.801
all the other good stuff, a better world?

00:21:37.801 --> 00:21:40.670
So I'm going to come back
to the chocolate sauce

00:21:40.670 --> 00:21:43.940
from time to time during
the next few classes,

00:21:43.940 --> 00:21:48.732
just to remind you how
it's really happening.

00:21:48.732 --> 00:21:52.149
Because when we discuss seven bad options

00:21:54.020 --> 00:21:57.860
for how cause and effect really happens,

00:21:57.860 --> 00:22:02.460
we have to remember to
forget the chocolate sauce.

00:22:02.460 --> 00:22:05.452
We have to remember to
forget the chocolate sauce.

00:22:05.452 --> 00:22:07.670
We can't talk about karma.

00:22:07.670 --> 00:22:11.192
We can't talk about things coming from me.

00:22:11.192 --> 00:22:15.581
When we say self-existent,
we're talking about

00:22:15.581 --> 00:22:19.498
independent of my luminous image. Got it?

00:22:20.541 --> 00:22:22.461
And you've got to remember that.

00:22:22.461 --> 00:22:26.929
When all these seven options
are all self-existent,

00:22:26.929 --> 00:22:27.762
RANG BZHIN GYIS YOD PA

00:22:27.762 --> 00:22:29.012
he keeps saying that

00:22:29.012 --> 00:22:30.922
over and over again.

00:22:30.922 --> 00:22:32.961
And you start to not see it anymore

00:22:32.961 --> 00:22:37.570
because he keeps repeating it,
but you've got to say that.

00:22:37.570 --> 00:22:38.459
You've got to say that.

00:22:38.459 --> 00:22:40.490
These are seven bad options

00:22:40.490 --> 00:22:43.082
because they all involve cause and effect

00:22:43.082 --> 00:22:44.792
which is coming from its own side,

00:22:44.792 --> 00:22:47.962
which is coming this way.

00:22:47.962 --> 00:22:51.170
All right, so don't forget
the chocolate sauce.

00:22:51.170 --> 00:22:52.003
I don't.

00:22:54.290 --> 00:22:57.850
I'm going to throw in
some Sanskrit words here

00:22:57.850 --> 00:23:00.362
that I think are helpful.

00:23:00.362 --> 00:23:03.409
I'm trying to limit these words.

00:23:03.409 --> 00:23:06.402
I'm trying to stick to
about 20 words or something,

00:23:06.402 --> 00:23:08.621
because I don't want to overwhelm you

00:23:08.621 --> 00:23:10.442
and I also don't want to give you a word

00:23:10.442 --> 00:23:12.050
that you're never going to use

00:23:12.050 --> 00:23:13.381
or that you're never going to see.

00:23:13.381 --> 00:23:15.729
I want to give you the
really important ones

00:23:15.729 --> 00:23:20.192
that are kind of like tools
that you have to have.

00:23:20.192 --> 00:23:23.261
So one word that I'd
like to talk about now

00:23:23.261 --> 00:23:25.802
is called 'samgati'.

00:23:25.802 --> 00:23:28.162
The Tibetan is
LHAN CIG PHRAD PA

00:23:28.162 --> 00:23:29.560
LHAN CIG PHRAD PA means

00:23:29.560 --> 00:23:32.352
PHRAD PA means to make contact.

00:23:32.352 --> 00:23:35.223
LHAN CIG means same place and same time.

00:23:35.223 --> 00:23:37.873
So that, I call it the crucial moment

00:23:37.873 --> 00:23:40.971
when cause and result
supposedly make contact,

00:23:40.971 --> 00:23:43.325
like the seed and the tree.

00:23:43.325 --> 00:23:47.102
There's a special tiny point of contact,

00:23:47.102 --> 00:23:50.685
which a mathematician
would say is a point,

00:23:52.718 --> 00:23:56.853
a point with no width,

00:23:56.853 --> 00:24:00.653
a theoretical point, point of contact.

00:24:00.653 --> 00:24:02.892
So that's called
LHAN CIG PHRAD PA

00:24:02.892 --> 00:24:03.973
They touch each other.

00:24:03.973 --> 00:24:07.473
Somewhere the seed touches the tree.

00:24:09.362 --> 00:24:12.610
And the 'gati' you know from Heart Sutra.

00:24:12.610 --> 00:24:13.610
What's that?

00:24:14.618 --> 00:24:17.050
"gati gati paragati
parasamgati bodhi svaha".

00:24:17.050 --> 00:24:18.250
Yeah, go, go, go.

00:24:18.250 --> 00:24:20.917
Go, go, go. Really go. Super go.

00:24:24.711 --> 00:24:26.264
So gati, and then that comes into

00:24:26.264 --> 00:24:29.228
the word go in English.

00:24:29.228 --> 00:24:30.478
So that's easy.

00:24:32.345 --> 00:24:33.875
/gam is the full root

00:24:33.875 --> 00:24:37.507
and come comes from that
also, if you're interested.

00:24:37.507 --> 00:24:40.714
The other word I'd like you to learn

00:24:40.714 --> 00:24:45.714
is drstva. And that means seen

00:24:45.897 --> 00:24:48.363
or a seeing.

00:24:49.494 --> 00:24:54.054
We're going to discuss it, as I mentioned,

00:24:54.054 --> 00:24:56.574
in the sense of anticipation

00:24:56.574 --> 00:24:59.323
or the potential for a result and a cause,

00:24:59.323 --> 00:25:01.530
because if you don't feel comfortable

00:25:01.530 --> 00:25:05.379
with results stopping and
then the cause starting,

00:25:05.379 --> 00:25:07.970
would you feel more
comfortable with saying

00:25:07.970 --> 00:25:10.690
the cause anticipates the result?

00:25:10.690 --> 00:25:12.300
Would you feel more comfortable that way?

00:25:12.300 --> 00:25:17.300
That somehow the result is
anticipated by the cause.

00:25:17.998 --> 00:25:21.710
Does that make you more comfortable?

00:25:21.710 --> 00:25:24.269
He's going to discuss that possibility.

00:25:24.269 --> 00:25:25.859
He doesn't say the word anticipate,

00:25:25.859 --> 00:25:28.270
he says within sight of.

00:25:28.270 --> 00:25:30.510
Is the result within sight of the cause?

00:25:30.510 --> 00:25:33.268
Is the cause somehow
anticipating the result?

00:25:33.268 --> 00:25:36.400
And the result is a little
farther away than touching,

00:25:36.400 --> 00:25:38.280
but it's still there.

00:25:38.280 --> 00:25:40.891
Not yet, but it's there.

00:25:40.891 --> 00:25:43.510
It's kind of like potential.

00:25:43.510 --> 00:25:47.091
And I like this root, the
Indo-European is /derk,

00:25:47.091 --> 00:25:49.289
it's not dork.

00:25:49.289 --> 00:25:52.620
'Derk' means to see in Indo-European

00:25:52.620 --> 00:25:54.950
and the word dragon comes from that

00:25:54.950 --> 00:25:59.950
because a dragon is, means
the one with the evil eye.

00:25:59.981 --> 00:26:03.569
The word dragon means the
one with the evil eye.

00:26:03.569 --> 00:26:06.569
It means the one with the eye.

00:26:07.520 --> 00:26:11.350
I did my three year retreat
in the Dragoon Mountains,

00:26:11.350 --> 00:26:13.672
and I was curious whether that was related

00:26:13.672 --> 00:26:18.419
to dragon and it is, somehow.

00:26:18.419 --> 00:26:19.740
I don't remember why.

00:26:19.740 --> 00:26:24.657
But you can look it up. It
means a special kind of soldier.

00:26:25.730 --> 00:26:28.888
A sentry, in a sense, maybe
the one with the eyes.

00:26:30.859 --> 00:26:33.339
The last word I'd like to
discuss here in the Sanskrit

00:26:33.339 --> 00:26:36.189
is 'śūnya', say śūnya-

00:26:37.073 --> 00:26:39.754
Long U, śūnya

00:26:39.754 --> 00:26:43.171
which means STONG, which means devoid of,

00:26:44.627 --> 00:26:46.315
and it requires the instrumental.

00:26:46.315 --> 00:26:48.982
So in English you say,

00:26:49.835 --> 00:26:54.835
this fresh tissue is devoid of boogers.

00:26:55.495 --> 00:26:58.002
Now it's not devoid of boogers.

00:26:58.002 --> 00:26:59.354
Just that devoid means,

00:26:59.354 --> 00:27:02.854
I was trying to get some excuse to use it.

00:27:03.834 --> 00:27:05.844
So in English you say devoid of.

00:27:05.844 --> 00:27:08.364
It means that it's a fresh tissue

00:27:08.364 --> 00:27:12.864
and it doesn't have any
other things inside yet.

00:27:13.714 --> 00:27:18.415
But in the Asian languages,
Tibetan and Sanskrit,

00:27:18.415 --> 00:27:20.282
you have to use the instrumental.

00:27:20.282 --> 00:27:21.615
'Devoid by'.

00:27:22.923 --> 00:27:25.644
Just remember that, because
it's going to come in handy.

00:27:25.644 --> 00:27:29.727
You don't say devoid
of, you say devoid by.

00:27:31.364 --> 00:27:36.364
For example,
SNABS BUS @DRING@ MED STONG BA

00:27:37.375 --> 00:27:42.086
means devoid by boogers.

00:27:42.086 --> 00:27:44.544
And not devoid of boogers.

00:27:44.544 --> 00:27:47.627
I knew you wanted to know that.

00:27:50.542 --> 00:27:51.641
But the problem is here,

00:27:51.641 --> 00:27:53.876
he's going to use 'STONG'
in two different senses.

00:27:53.876 --> 00:27:55.367
I looked up the word today

00:27:55.367 --> 00:27:56.993
because I couldn't remember it.

00:27:56.993 --> 00:27:57.910
Equivocate.

00:27:58.777 --> 00:28:02.426
He's going to use the word
empty in two different meanings,

00:28:02.426 --> 00:28:05.126
and he kind of cheats.

00:28:05.126 --> 00:28:08.177
He says, and we'll see why,

00:28:08.177 --> 00:28:12.556
one thing he says "cause
can't be empty of the result

00:28:12.556 --> 00:28:16.467
"because an empty result
would be like empty,

00:28:16.467 --> 00:28:21.276
"would be like NAM MKHA'I ME TOG,"

00:28:21.276 --> 00:28:24.348
a flower sprouting in mid air,

00:28:24.348 --> 00:28:29.348
with no roots, no water, no
soil, nothing, just boop.

00:28:29.617 --> 00:28:33.367
He uses it in a sense
of the void as a space,

00:28:35.575 --> 00:28:37.307
and then he's going to switch

00:28:37.307 --> 00:28:38.865
between two kinds of void.

00:28:38.865 --> 00:28:40.606
So just be aware.

00:28:40.606 --> 00:28:42.968
When you say STONG PA,

00:28:42.968 --> 00:28:44.976
or STONG PA NYID,

00:28:44.976 --> 00:28:49.976
you mean the void, or
emptiness of self-existence.

00:28:50.128 --> 00:28:53.454
But when you just say STONG, 'śūnya' here,

00:28:53.454 --> 00:28:57.843
śūnya, not 'śūnyatā', not emptiness,

00:28:57.843 --> 00:29:00.760
but just empty, then it's not clear

00:29:01.596 --> 00:29:03.334
what you're talking about.

00:29:03.334 --> 00:29:07.073
Could be empty mind. It
could be an empty cup.

00:29:07.073 --> 00:29:11.323
Could be empty of self-existence.
We don't know yet.

00:29:11.323 --> 00:29:14.153
I'm just saying be aware,

00:29:14.153 --> 00:29:16.736
śūnya, by itself, is ambiguous.

00:29:17.833 --> 00:29:21.821
It needs some, you need someone
to tell you which śūnya.

00:29:21.821 --> 00:29:26.061
It has a long U, which
often changes to AU.

00:29:26.061 --> 00:29:30.581
All Sanskrit vowels have
three degrees of strength:

00:29:30.581 --> 00:29:32.998
short U, long U, and then AU.

00:29:34.173 --> 00:29:37.006
And then AU becomes OW.

00:29:38.550 --> 00:29:42.880
And the AU often changes to AV.

00:29:42.880 --> 00:29:47.629
AU as a combination in ancient
Sanskrit, Greek, Latin,

00:29:47.629 --> 00:29:51.079
often changes to AV, so you get,

00:29:51.079 --> 00:29:56.012
shu becomes cave, as a cavity.

00:29:57.158 --> 00:30:00.850
Because the U changed,
the AU changed to AV.

00:30:00.850 --> 00:30:05.708
And the C changed, became
a hard K from a soft S,

00:30:05.708 --> 00:30:09.208
and it became cave, or cavity.

00:30:10.050 --> 00:30:13.732
Vault comes from that.
Swell comes from that

00:30:13.732 --> 00:30:15.591
and hole comes from that,

00:30:15.591 --> 00:30:18.618
because H's come from K and like that.

00:30:18.618 --> 00:30:23.618
Excavate, cumulous clouds,
church comes from that

00:30:24.050 --> 00:30:28.133
because a churches were
originally perceived as

00:30:28.999 --> 00:30:31.518
mighty things with might inside.

00:30:31.518 --> 00:30:35.988
Empty inside, like the power
to just grow, grow, grow.

00:30:35.988 --> 00:30:40.980
Churches were seen as places
of hot air expanding.

00:30:42.159 --> 00:30:43.570
Something like that.

00:30:43.570 --> 00:30:46.320
No, power expanding, not hot air.

00:30:47.371 --> 00:30:50.739
Those words are going to come in handy.

00:30:50.739 --> 00:30:52.851
I'll say them again.

00:30:52.851 --> 00:30:57.518
'Samgati', which means is there
ever a meeting of the two.

00:30:58.590 --> 00:31:00.885
'Drstva', which means can we see

00:31:00.885 --> 00:31:03.394
or anticipate a result coming,

00:31:03.394 --> 00:31:05.485
even in the time of the cause.

00:31:05.485 --> 00:31:06.735
And then 'śūnya',

00:31:08.463 --> 00:31:11.453
when we say the cause
or the result is empty,

00:31:11.453 --> 00:31:13.754
what do we mean?

00:31:13.754 --> 00:31:14.921
Here we go.

00:31:16.392 --> 00:31:17.458
Remember that we're going through

00:31:17.458 --> 00:31:19.934
seven combinations of possibilities,

00:31:19.934 --> 00:31:21.894
and here is the second one.

00:31:21.894 --> 00:31:25.155
The result is triggered, and
a lot of the possibilities

00:31:25.155 --> 00:31:28.133
are questions: is it this or is it this?

00:31:28.133 --> 00:31:30.934
Possibility number two is:

00:31:30.934 --> 00:31:35.663
is the result triggered within
sight of the cause or not?

00:31:35.663 --> 00:31:39.545
Is the result triggered
in sight of the cause,

00:31:39.545 --> 00:31:41.334
in view of the cause,

00:31:41.334 --> 00:31:43.785
which kind of means presence of the cause?

00:31:43.785 --> 00:31:45.385
Is the cause still standing around

00:31:45.385 --> 00:31:47.715
by the time the result came out?

00:31:47.715 --> 00:31:52.003
And is the cause able to see the result?

00:31:52.003 --> 00:31:55.835
Can the result, in a sense,
be anticipated by the cause?

00:31:55.835 --> 00:31:57.715
And here's his arguments.

00:31:57.715 --> 00:32:00.681
,RGYUS NI MTHONG DANG MA MTHONG BAR,

00:32:00.681 --> 00:32:01.545
,'BRAS BU SKYED PAR MI BYED DO,,

00:32:01.545 --> 00:32:03.128
He says both wrong.

00:32:05.025 --> 00:32:07.715
Neither is the result seen by the cause,

00:32:07.715 --> 00:32:10.246
nor is it not seen by the cause.

00:32:10.246 --> 00:32:12.237
RGYUS NI RANG GI 'BRAS BU

00:32:12.237 --> 00:32:15.870
MTHONG NAS SAM MA MTHONG BAR

00:32:15.870 --> 00:32:18.946
It's not that the cause
can anticipate the result,

00:32:18.946 --> 00:32:21.153
because
MTHONG NAS GRUB ZIN PAS

00:32:21.153 --> 00:32:23.524
when you talk about seeing something,

00:32:23.524 --> 00:32:28.524
the thing you see should have
come into existence already.

00:32:28.546 --> 00:32:30.794
When you talk about seeing something.

00:32:30.794 --> 00:32:32.805
If you see something, it should have come

00:32:32.805 --> 00:32:34.564
into existence already.

00:32:34.564 --> 00:32:37.604
Even as a potential, it should
have come into existence

00:32:37.604 --> 00:32:39.937
as a potential result.

00:32:41.333 --> 00:32:43.474
And there wouldn't be any purpose

00:32:43.474 --> 00:32:45.815
to the thing happening again.

00:32:45.815 --> 00:32:47.944
If a thing could be anticipated,

00:32:47.944 --> 00:32:51.185
if you could see a result in the future

00:32:51.185 --> 00:32:53.352
that's likely or probable,

00:32:54.195 --> 00:32:57.101
then in a way you've already
made contact with that result,

00:32:57.101 --> 00:32:58.410
and there wouldn't be any reason

00:32:58.410 --> 00:33:01.442
for it to grow again.

00:33:01.442 --> 00:33:05.192
For there to be another
result happen, just that one.

00:33:05.192 --> 00:33:06.871
If the result didn't happen,

00:33:06.871 --> 00:33:09.991
there's no way you could
anticipate, you couldn't see it.

00:33:09.991 --> 00:33:14.042
If it didn't have any

00:33:14.042 --> 00:33:18.752
existential status, then
you couldn't see it.

00:33:18.752 --> 00:33:22.032
If you could see it, then
it had existential status

00:33:22.032 --> 00:33:23.062
and there's no reason for it

00:33:23.062 --> 00:33:26.029
to happen again a second time.

00:33:30.312 --> 00:33:33.341
Now, if you said I saw a potential
result, that's different.

00:33:33.341 --> 00:33:36.912
But if you say I saw
the result, how's that?

00:33:36.912 --> 00:33:38.352
Inside out.

00:33:38.352 --> 00:33:43.344
And he says if the result is that solid,

00:33:45.630 --> 00:33:49.401
upcoming result is that
solid, then there's no reason

00:33:49.401 --> 00:33:52.300
for the cause to work
so hard to create it.

00:33:52.300 --> 00:33:55.367
And then he says the job,
the cause would have to apply

00:33:55.367 --> 00:33:59.201
for unemployment benefits, next picture.

00:34:01.409 --> 00:34:04.127
Like it wouldn't have, it's
job would be done already

00:34:04.127 --> 00:34:06.680
and it would have to, it would get fired

00:34:06.680 --> 00:34:09.940
because the job was already filled.

00:34:12.009 --> 00:34:15.325
RGYUS 'BRAS BU MA MTHONG BAR

00:34:15.325 --> 00:34:17.025
RANG BZHIN GYIS SKYED PAR MI BYED DE,

00:34:18.100 --> 00:34:22.030
But if you say the cause
cannot anticipate the result

00:34:22.030 --> 00:34:24.641
and cannot see the result coming,

00:34:24.641 --> 00:34:26.116
SKYED NA RGYU GCIG GIS KYANG

00:34:26.116 --> 00:34:28.173
'BRAS BU THAMS CAD CIG CAR SKYED

00:34:29.139 --> 00:34:31.369
If it's not necessary to be able

00:34:31.369 --> 00:34:35.307
to see a potential result
in the time of the cause,

00:34:35.307 --> 00:34:37.398
and if it's not possible,

00:34:37.398 --> 00:34:39.907
then it makes sense that
all possible results

00:34:39.907 --> 00:34:42.449
would be possible from a single cause.

00:34:42.449 --> 00:34:43.798
Because there's no reason why

00:34:43.798 --> 00:34:46.569
one would be more likely than another.

00:34:46.569 --> 00:34:49.067
If one result were not
more likely than another,

00:34:49.067 --> 00:34:52.431
then it would make sense
that a single cause

00:34:52.431 --> 00:34:55.551
could trigger any result.

00:34:55.551 --> 00:34:58.759
If there's no more likelihood
of a similar result

00:34:58.759 --> 00:35:00.551
than a non-similar result.

00:35:00.551 --> 00:35:02.809
Because you can't anticipate
it because you can't see it,

00:35:02.809 --> 00:35:03.642
because it doesn't have

00:35:03.642 --> 00:35:07.142
any existential status in the present yet.

00:35:09.770 --> 00:35:13.898
We got a picture for that

00:35:13.898 --> 00:35:15.747
and I forget what the picture was.

00:35:15.747 --> 00:35:18.650
Oh yeah, he says all possible results

00:35:18.650 --> 00:35:21.010
would be triggered by a single cause

00:35:21.010 --> 00:35:25.010
if a cause couldn't, if
you could not anticipate

00:35:25.010 --> 00:35:27.920
a particular result
from a particular cause,

00:35:27.920 --> 00:35:32.895
then all possible results would
result from a single cause.

00:35:34.338 --> 00:35:35.770
If there was no more likelihood

00:35:35.770 --> 00:35:39.120
that one result would
happen than another result,

00:35:39.120 --> 00:35:41.058
then one cause would create,

00:35:41.058 --> 00:35:45.080
one wheat seed would create
a whole field of wheat.

00:35:45.080 --> 00:35:47.218
Because there's no more likelihood

00:35:47.218 --> 00:35:49.690
that it would create one stalk of wheat

00:35:49.690 --> 00:35:52.469
than any other stalk of wheat.

00:35:52.469 --> 00:35:54.673
There wouldn't be any more likelihood.

00:35:54.673 --> 00:35:56.942
Odds would be canceled.

00:35:56.942 --> 00:36:00.141
If there was no amount of the result

00:36:00.141 --> 00:36:02.502
present in the time of the cause,

00:36:02.502 --> 00:36:07.502
then the probability of all
things happening is 100%.

00:36:07.961 --> 00:36:12.212
And the probability of
one thing happening is 0%.

00:36:12.212 --> 00:36:13.582
Because you can't anticipate it,

00:36:13.582 --> 00:36:16.052
because it doesn't have
any kind of existence yet,

00:36:16.052 --> 00:36:18.052
not even as a potential.

00:36:19.022 --> 00:36:22.702
Because there's no relationship.
They're totally separate.

00:36:22.702 --> 00:36:23.913
They don't share any kind,

00:36:23.913 --> 00:36:27.172
they're not holding hands anywhere.

00:36:27.172 --> 00:36:28.672
Are you all right?

00:36:29.621 --> 00:36:32.422
By the way,

00:36:32.422 --> 00:36:34.191
here's a tiny RANG LUGS.

00:36:34.191 --> 00:36:35.993
Tim, what's a RANG LUGS?

00:36:35.993 --> 00:36:38.910
Sorry, I have allergies, I'm sorry.

00:36:42.202 --> 00:36:43.035
Say again?

00:36:45.053 --> 00:36:47.654
Yeah, RANG LUGS is, LUGS,

00:36:47.654 --> 00:36:50.044
and here's a rare occurrence where he says

00:36:50.044 --> 00:36:52.051
"what do we think?"

00:36:52.051 --> 00:36:54.521
And I complain that he hadn't bring up,

00:36:54.521 --> 00:36:56.830
he didn't bring up ice cream yet.

00:36:56.830 --> 00:37:01.830
And he has a lame RANG LUGS here.

00:37:02.890 --> 00:37:06.932
RANG LUGS LA NI RGYUS 'BRAS
BU MA MTHONG BAR SKYED KYANG

00:37:06.932 --> 00:37:09.042
Our position, if you want to know,

00:37:09.042 --> 00:37:14.042
is that the cause does not create a result

00:37:14.194 --> 00:37:19.077
which is anticipated,
but still that's not,

00:37:22.320 --> 00:37:23.853
that doesn't contradict saying

00:37:23.853 --> 00:37:27.520
it couldn't create a
cause in and of itself.

00:37:29.143 --> 00:37:30.682
Can you anticipate a result?

00:37:30.682 --> 00:37:31.641
No.

00:37:31.641 --> 00:37:34.314
Does that mean it has to create a cause?

00:37:34.314 --> 00:37:36.863
That the cause has to create
a result in and of itself?

00:37:36.863 --> 00:37:39.943
Not either.

00:37:39.943 --> 00:37:44.242
It's not contradictory to say
a cause has no self nature,

00:37:44.242 --> 00:37:48.825
if it does not anticipate its result.

00:37:51.714 --> 00:37:53.622
I'll say it again.

00:37:53.622 --> 00:37:58.572
If us, if our side says that
there is no anticipation

00:37:59.643 --> 00:38:02.843
of a particular result
by a particular cause,

00:38:02.843 --> 00:38:06.370
that doesn't contradict us also saying

00:38:06.370 --> 00:38:08.313
that the cause doesn't automatically lead

00:38:08.313 --> 00:38:10.230
to a particular result.

00:38:12.211 --> 00:38:14.891
And then he doesn't help us. He goes on.

00:38:14.891 --> 00:38:17.593
And that's only Choney Lama being nice.

00:38:17.593 --> 00:38:21.233
There's nothing in Nagarjuna about it.

00:38:22.382 --> 00:38:24.222
Listen to the recording three times.

00:38:24.222 --> 00:38:29.222
Option number three of seven,

00:38:29.662 --> 00:38:32.443
the result is triggered

00:38:32.443 --> 00:38:33.971
by contact with the cause.

00:38:33.971 --> 00:38:38.050
Let's examine,
BRTAGS PA ... BRTAGS PA

00:38:38.050 --> 00:38:40.763
let's examine whether or not

00:38:40.763 --> 00:38:43.331
the result is triggered
through contact with the cause.

00:38:43.331 --> 00:38:45.531
Is there contact between
the cause and the result,

00:38:45.531 --> 00:38:46.871
or not?

00:38:46.871 --> 00:38:48.929
That's what we're going to look at.

00:38:48.929 --> 00:38:52.403
And this is long, this is
four verses in the Sanskrit

00:38:52.403 --> 00:38:56.062
which is unusually long.

00:38:56.062 --> 00:38:58.571
And there's a lot of options here.

00:38:58.571 --> 00:39:01.371
We're going to start them, and by the way,

00:39:01.371 --> 00:39:04.954
one of the lines of
the Tibetan is missing,

00:39:05.851 --> 00:39:08.651
which makes it more interesting.

00:39:08.651 --> 00:39:12.811
And I went and recovered
it from the Tengyur,

00:39:12.811 --> 00:39:16.233
due to the fact that we have ALL,

00:39:16.233 --> 00:39:19.066
which typed in the entire Tengyur,

00:39:20.153 --> 00:39:25.013
which recovered the only
Tengyur outside of Tibet.

00:39:25.013 --> 00:39:28.846
The only one in India,
that ALL was the first,

00:39:32.503 --> 00:39:36.503
ALL brought the first Tengyur out of Tibet

00:39:36.503 --> 00:39:38.442
in modern times.

00:39:38.442 --> 00:39:41.092
And that was quite an adventure story.

00:39:41.092 --> 00:39:44.143
We should tell it some day.

00:39:44.143 --> 00:39:45.642
Okay, I'll tell you,
we have a few minutes.

00:39:48.053 --> 00:39:51.823
There's a printery called
Derge in east Tibet

00:39:51.823 --> 00:39:56.456
and I can talk about the Red Guards.

00:39:57.382 --> 00:39:59.965
During the cultural revolution,

00:40:00.863 --> 00:40:03.773
the Red Guards came to burn that library.

00:40:03.773 --> 00:40:08.573
And there was a monk who was
trying to protect the library

00:40:08.573 --> 00:40:12.071
and it's like an army
facing a single monk.

00:40:12.071 --> 00:40:14.471
And he had this inspiration.

00:40:14.471 --> 00:40:18.971
He took all his clothes off,
and he went and got and ax

00:40:19.893 --> 00:40:22.723
and he danced around the door
of the library with his ax

00:40:22.723 --> 00:40:24.303
and he said anyone who comes in here

00:40:24.303 --> 00:40:26.091
will lose their head.

00:40:26.091 --> 00:40:28.685
And they called the general of the army.

00:40:28.685 --> 00:40:30.573
This is the story I heard.

00:40:30.573 --> 00:40:33.114
And he came up, he
said, "What's going on?"

00:40:33.114 --> 00:40:35.534
They said, "We want to burn this library,

00:40:35.534 --> 00:40:37.355
"but there's this crazy
monk staying there.

00:40:37.355 --> 00:40:39.923
"He's got a, he's threatening
to cut off anyone's head

00:40:39.923 --> 00:40:44.353
"who comes, and he's got
his penis hanging out

00:40:44.353 --> 00:40:46.054
"and it's weird.

00:40:46.054 --> 00:40:48.199
What should we do, should we
just shoot him in the head?"

00:40:48.199 --> 00:40:49.360
And he said "No, no, leave him,

00:40:49.360 --> 00:40:53.328
we'll do it later and
we'll burn it later."

00:40:53.328 --> 00:40:55.030
And then they forgot to burn it.

00:40:55.030 --> 00:40:57.160
They never got back to it,

00:40:57.160 --> 00:41:01.488
and so those blocks
from the 1700s survived.

00:41:01.488 --> 00:41:05.488
210 volumes which, times 1,000.

00:41:05.488 --> 00:41:08.247
210,000 times two, because you have to do

00:41:08.247 --> 00:41:09.857
to front side and the back side,

00:41:09.857 --> 00:41:12.606
now you're talking half a million blocks.

00:41:12.606 --> 00:41:14.288
Because there's separate
block for the front side

00:41:14.288 --> 00:41:15.990
and a separate block for the back side.

00:41:15.990 --> 00:41:18.047
Sometimes they don't get it right,

00:41:18.047 --> 00:41:20.028
they put the back of page
three on the back of page,

00:41:20.028 --> 00:41:22.695
or on the front of page seven.

00:41:22.695 --> 00:41:25.857
And the backs don't have page numbers,

00:41:25.857 --> 00:41:26.988
but that makes life interesting.

00:41:26.988 --> 00:41:30.687
Anyway, half a million blocks survived,

00:41:30.687 --> 00:41:33.829
and no copy was printed

00:41:34.770 --> 00:41:38.186
for about 30 years

00:41:38.186 --> 00:41:41.247
from the blocks from the 1700s.

00:41:41.247 --> 00:41:46.005
And then ALL made it happen

00:41:47.497 --> 00:41:52.480
through various means. And we
paid a huge amount of money

00:41:54.076 --> 00:41:56.716
to unspecified account,

00:41:56.716 --> 00:42:01.133
and we waited for two years.
And the books showed up,

00:42:02.367 --> 00:42:03.367
210 volumes.

00:42:04.819 --> 00:42:07.720
It's priceless. They're priceless.

00:42:07.720 --> 00:42:12.087
And then JB's crew proceeded to type in

00:42:12.921 --> 00:42:17.828
the 410,000 pages, and they finished.

00:42:17.828 --> 00:42:22.428
420,000 pages. They finished.

00:42:22.428 --> 00:42:25.128
And that's why we have it.

00:42:25.128 --> 00:42:27.595
And that's why I can replace a line

00:42:27.595 --> 00:42:31.749
that was left off of this commentary.

00:42:31.749 --> 00:42:36.169
Yay JB. Let's give him a hand.

00:42:36.169 --> 00:42:37.009
Good story.

00:42:37.009 --> 00:42:41.496
Anyway, we're going to
continue in the next class.

00:42:41.496 --> 00:42:43.456
Which option are we on you guys?

00:42:43.456 --> 00:42:46.837
We're on option number three. Yeah.

00:42:46.837 --> 00:42:47.827
We still got a ways to go.

00:42:47.827 --> 00:42:50.757
By the way, these options are long,

00:42:50.757 --> 00:42:54.005
and we're going to, when you
get impatient with a text,

00:42:54.005 --> 00:42:55.637
slow down.

00:42:55.637 --> 00:42:57.827
When you get impatient with a text,

00:42:57.827 --> 00:43:00.757
and when you're thinking
you wish it would go faster,

00:43:00.757 --> 00:43:04.840
that's the time, if you
really want to be a Yogi,

00:43:05.865 --> 00:43:07.774
you purposefully slow yourself down

00:43:07.774 --> 00:43:12.093
and you digest it with pleasure,

00:43:12.093 --> 00:43:14.496
with shamatha, 'śamatha'.

